{#intro}
# Carve in CodeMirror

## Text and formatting

This is *bold text*, /italic text/ and /*both at once*/.
You can add _underlining_, ~strikethrough~ and =highlighting=.
Or write H{,2,}O, x{^2^}, `code` and $`a + b = c`.

A link to an [example](https://example.com), a footnote [^note]
and a cross-reference to the section </#intro>.

%% Comments do not mix with regular markup.

## Citations and bibliography

One source [@smith2020], several [see @smith2020, p. 4; -@jones2019]
and an integral citation [+@jones2019].

[@smith2020]: {author="Smith" year="2020"} Smith, J. *A Study of Carve*.
[@jones2019]: {author="Jones" year="2019"} Jones, A. /Notes on Markup/.

Type @ inside a citation group and press Ctrl+Space to choose a source.

